  "scope": [
    "One source, one clone, one GC, 1-2 statements (optional first overwrite), at most two transaction retries.",
    "RetainSnapshots=1 uses the captured head (zero retention); 3 models ByNumOfSnapshotsToKeep(3), including directory truncation and the candidate predecessor.",
    "Delta is segment_block_timestamp minus snapshot_timestamp; logical time samples 1 and 3.",
    "SplitAdvance=false keeps the atomic concurrent replacement/append baseline. True splits its metadata read, physical snapshot read/time sample, block/segment/snapshot writes, Meta precheck and CAS; a conflict ends this bounded attempt (no second-writer retry).",
    "Snapshot UUID tie ordering samples two rankings. AdvanceSource and AdvanceSampleTime sample wall time two ticks later; no arbitrary clock jumps or skew.",
    "decorate_snapshot makes every buffered statement point to the transaction base, not the previous buffered statement. Data refs still include earlier statements.",
    "CLONE AT SNAPSHOT captures source metadata, walks prev links and rereads the selected snapshot. Up to three source-version refreshes keep the snapshot ID fixed.",
    "CloneCacheHits models a remote cache retaining that history after GC; false uses physical reads. Rust MAINTENANCE bypasses disk cache but retains memory cache. This single-GC model checks existence at GC reads: all marking/protected-segment reads precede its only deletion phase, so prior/concurrent-GC stale-cache behavior is NOT covered. No eviction model.",
    "Exact atomic storage listings, immutable objects; clone failures retain staged bindings. No DROP, FLASHBACK, tags, restart, clone writes, multi-table commits or concurrent/second GC. Streaming list pagination and partial delete errors remain outside scope."
  ],
  "audit": [
    "2026-11-05 source review: HEAD still 29b08e94e01f0a3462815a4628ce05fac02a7b2f; no staged/unstaged tracked-code diff, only these four untracked model/docs files. No source-version drift. Rechecked clone staging, LVT CAS/rescan, timestamp sampling, buffered ancestry and retention selection.",
    "Coverage gap: atomic AdvanceSource excluded a second writer's partially written objects and precheck/CAS windows. SplitAdvance refines this actor in the same model; original safety invariants and baseline cases are unchanged. Conflict is an incomplete writer attempt, not a claim that Rust always aborts rather than retries.",
    "Cache-scope correction: catalog/src/cache_policy.rs::MAINTENANCE still reads/fills memory. The old GC-physical-read description was an abstraction, not the implementation policy; do not reuse it to claim multi-GC cache safety.",
    "Retained-history normal failures with w2.prev=w1 were model errors: decorate_snapshot writes w2.prev=base. Same-HEAD native SQL confirmed the collapsed history; keep both retained cases as normal safety checks.",
    "Same-HEAD licensed native runs: count retention kept live rows and later reclaimed buffered snapshots; a stale cross-node writer after first CLONE + VACUUM aborted on the txn-begin timestamp check. No production defect confirmed."
  ],
